}(document,"script","exco-player"));
</script>





<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In Nekome: Nazi Hunter, players step into the role of Vano Nastasu, a young Romani man consumed by grief after the brutal murder of his family by Nazi soldiers. The game follows Vano’s transformation from hunted to hunter as he embarks on a violent personal odyssey of revenge across war-torn Europe.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The game is part of a series of smaller, more focused games that don&#8217;t require huge budgets. ProbablyMonsters raised a lot of money, but it <a href="https://gamesbeat.com/probablymonsters-reveals-its-first-two-games-storm-lancers-and-ire-a-prologue/">pivoted to smaller games</a> that take less time to get done yet still hold promise for great success. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/02_Nek_Announce_Screenshot-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-315968" srcset="https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/02_Nek_Announce_Screenshot-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/02_Nek_Announce_Screenshot-300x169.jpg 300w, https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/02_Nek_Announce_Screenshot-768x432.jpg 768w, https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/02_Nek_Announce_Screenshot.jpg 1200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Nekome: Nazi Hunter is a single-player game. Source: ProbablyMonsters</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">[<a href="https://youtu.be/cfi7rGaz3gg">View Nekome: Nazi Hunter Teaser Trailer Here</a>]</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nekome: Nazi Hunter approaches the Second World War from the personal perspective of Vano as he exacts revenge for the sadistic murders. </p><div id="div-gpt-ad-1752171790614-6" style="width: 300px; min-height: 250px;">
  <script>
    googletag.cmd.push(function() { googletag.display('div-gpt-ad-1752171790614-6'); });
  </script>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Players scout enemy routes, plan their assaults, and strike with precision in a mix of stealth and brutal, up-close combat where every attack is personal and every kill is meaningful. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/03_Nek_Announce_Screenshot-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-315969" srcset="https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/03_Nek_Announce_Screenshot-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/03_Nek_Announce_Screenshot-300x169.jpg 300w, https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/03_Nek_Announce_Screenshot-768x432.jpg 768w, https://gamesbeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/03_Nek_Announce_Screenshot.jpg 1200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Nekome: Nazi Hunter has visceral combat. Source: ProbablyMonsters</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The game is inspired by grindhouse cinema and features visceral combat with grounded finishing moves, coming together in a symphony of violence where every encounter carries lasting consequences.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Players can also join the community on <a href="https://discord.gg/playnekome">Discord</a>. Nekome: Nazi Hunter is rated M for Mature. More information about the game will be revealed at GDC in March 2026.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>

